 - `0179_stamp_criteria_engine` — Stamp Wave 3: activates the dormant stamp_definitions.criteria jsonb via a versioned rule engine. Flag `stamp_criteria_engine_enabled` (default FALSE). Seeds parity criteria onto community_connector/popular_traveler/travel_influencer/road_warrior/frequent_flyer (mirror existing hard-coded thresholds — no behavior change), and adds 4 event-category definitions (foodie_explorer, music_lover, outdoor_adventurer, event_regular) as is_active=FALSE automatic criteria stamps. Engine is additive: gates awards only when a definition has authored criteria AND the flag is on; hard-coded award sites remain authority otherwise.
 - `0180_activate_event_category_stamps` — Stamp Wave 3 follow-up: activates foodie_explorer/music_lover/outdoor_adventurer/event_regular (0179 left them inactive). Still gated by stamp_criteria_engine_enabled (evaluateAndAwardCriteria no-ops when off), so the engine flag becomes the single switch. RSVP-going now derives event category context (category+tags keyword match) and evaluates these 4 via the criteria engine.
 - `0181_stamp_unified_view` — Stamp legacy unification (read-layer): flag stamp_unified_view_enabled (default FALSE). UnifiedStampService merges v1 passport_stamps (GPS) + v2 user_stamps (achievements) into one deduped read collection (dedup by catalog_id backfilled by reconcile, else stamp_type|country|city; v2 wins ties). GET /stamps/me/unified always available; when flag ON the passport-card stampCount reports the deduped v1+v2 total instead of v1-only. NO schema change, NO data migration, both write paths untouched.
